1
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:07,183
(We’re going to hang out after this event.)

2
00:00:07,398 --> 00:00:08,455
(Wanna join us?)
NAWINA HOMECOMING

3
00:00:08,479 --> 00:00:09,679
I have somewhere I need to be.

4
00:00:09,844 --> 00:00:10,844
A funeral.

5
00:00:11,359 --> 00:00:12,999
It’s an old friend who meant a lot to me.

6
00:00:14,772 --> 00:00:16,972
There’s something I want to tell you before
anyone else.

7
00:00:17,181 --> 00:00:19,720
I’ve decided not to apply to law school anymore.

8
00:00:20,324 --> 00:00:21,000
Huh?

9
00:00:21,087 --> 00:00:23,760
At first, my dad was supposed to transfer
overseas for work,

10
00:00:24,154 --> 00:00:25,154
At first?

11
00:00:25,306 --> 00:00:27,640
But now I’m not moving anymore.

12
00:02:10,522 --> 00:02:13,106
(I’ve decided not to apply to law school anymore.)

13
00:02:13,821 --> 00:02:16,080
But now I’m not moving anymore.

14
00:02:16,850 --> 00:02:17,878
(Because of you.)

15
00:02:18,117 --> 00:02:20,406
- (I’ve had so much fun spending this semester with you.)
- ( Because of you.)

16
00:02:20,430 --> 00:02:22,811
(You were the one who told me that
if I wanted to draw, )

17
00:02:22,836 --> 00:02:23,537
(I should just do it instead of waiting.)

18
00:02:23,562 --> 00:02:24,882
Have you been studying that hard?

19
00:02:24,977 --> 00:02:26,600
You look like you didn’t get any sleep.

20
00:02:30,190 --> 00:02:31,360
I didn’t sleep very well.

21
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:33,440
Don’t worry too much about the exams.

22
00:02:33,888 --> 00:02:35,336
It’s not that serious.

23
00:02:56,113 --> 00:02:58,200
La la

24
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:06,160
(VEGETABLE AND FLOWER GARDEN]
(HOME ECONOMICS]

25
00:03:07,095 --> 00:03:07,803
Mr. Tin.

26
00:03:07,903 --> 00:03:08,903
Hey.

27
00:03:09,781 --> 00:03:10,781
Jiraphat.

28
00:03:12,816 --> 00:03:14,456
There’s no morning assembly today, right?

29
00:03:14,682 --> 00:03:16,000
Why did you come so early?

30
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:23,880
Is this the vegetable garden they have to finish
by the end of the semester?

31
00:03:25,782 --> 00:03:26,902
Do me a favor.

32
00:03:27,519 --> 00:03:29,439
Can you keep this from the junior high students?

33
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:33,280
You’ve been doing this every morning?

34
00:03:33,369 --> 00:03:37,160
Oh, no. We’ve been taking turns watering these plants.

35
00:03:37,851 --> 00:03:41,120
You know our school has so many activities.

36
00:03:41,236 --> 00:03:44,000
I do what I can to help the students.

37
00:04:04,821 --> 00:04:05,941
Hey, Jiraphat.

38
00:04:10,019 --> 00:04:12,200
Are you worried about Tyler and Phappim?

39
00:04:27,172 --> 00:04:31,200
Tyler’s father told me at the parent-teacher meeting

40
00:04:32,012 --> 00:04:34,532
that he would have his son withdraw
at the end of this semester.

41
00:04:35,547 --> 00:04:38,120
But a few days ago, he called to tell me

42
00:04:38,501 --> 00:04:39,756
that he’d changed his mind.

43
00:04:41,084 --> 00:04:43,640
As for Phappim, after returning from the school trip,

44
00:04:43,844 --> 00:04:47,240
she asked me to talk to her family.

45
00:04:48,530 --> 00:04:49,608
But you know what?

46
00:04:49,730 --> 00:04:53,470
Both of them…mentioned you.

47
00:04:55,167 --> 00:04:56,546
So I guessed you were involved.

48
00:05:00,549 --> 00:05:01,880
What are you afraid of, Jiraphat?

49
00:05:06,498 --> 00:05:07,498
I...

50
00:05:07,789 --> 00:05:11,501
Do you really think those two will decide
their own futures

51
00:05:12,198 --> 00:05:13,640
based only on what you say?

52
00:05:19,895 --> 00:05:21,000
Why worry?

53
00:05:21,429 --> 00:05:23,406
They don't even seem worried about it.

54
00:05:24,768 --> 00:05:26,440
No one knows the future.

55
00:05:28,754 --> 00:05:29,880
Someone might do.

56
00:05:30,352 --> 00:05:31,352
Hmm?

57
00:05:32,701 --> 00:05:36,400
What if the path they don't choose is
the better one?

58
00:05:37,144 --> 00:05:42,200
Well, life offers a million choices.

59
00:05:43,283 --> 00:05:45,960
Even if those two really do choose the wrong path,

60
00:05:47,946 --> 00:05:49,080
would you abandon them?

61
00:05:52,491 --> 00:05:53,491
I wouldn’t.

62
00:05:59,405 --> 00:06:02,000
When I found out I’d be the advisor for Class 7,

63
00:06:02,406 --> 00:06:04,280
you were the one I was most worried about.

64
00:06:05,091 --> 00:06:06,091
Me?

65
00:06:06,847 --> 00:06:08,781
Of course. In your first semester of Grade 10,

66
00:06:08,806 --> 00:06:10,880
you were in my history class, right?

67
00:06:11,589 --> 00:06:15,880
Mr. Narong told me you were the kind of student
who came late and left early.

68
00:06:16,554 --> 00:06:17,880
Never participated in activities.

69
00:06:18,669 --> 00:06:19,669
But you know what?

70
00:06:20,252 --> 00:06:21,360
In my class,

71
00:06:22,393 --> 00:06:25,000
you were the only one who always paid attention.

72
00:06:26,978 --> 00:06:29,280
And at last year’s science fair,

73
00:06:29,682 --> 00:06:33,680
I saw you cleaning up the equipment your classmates had left behind.

74
00:06:34,721 --> 00:06:38,480
So when Tyler asked me to put your name down
for the offering trays,

75
00:06:38,888 --> 00:06:40,848
I wasn’t trying to make things difficult for you.

76
00:06:42,516 --> 00:06:44,440
From everything I’ve observed about you,

77
00:06:46,630 --> 00:06:48,240
I just wanted all your classmates

78
00:06:48,953 --> 00:06:50,280
to remember the name Jiraphat.

79
00:07:03,566 --> 00:07:06,360
Does that smile mean you’re not worried anymore?

80
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:08,040
Thank you, sir.

81
00:07:08,204 --> 00:07:10,040
I’ll go then.

82
00:07:15,006 --> 00:07:16,526
Oh, wait, Jiraphat.

83
00:07:16,847 --> 00:07:17,847
Yes, sir?

84
00:07:17,938 --> 00:07:19,000
Can I ask you something?

85
00:07:21,760 --> 00:07:23,320
Are you close with the class president?

86
00:07:26,236 --> 00:07:28,680
Well…I guess I am.

87
00:07:29,407 --> 00:07:31,040
Are you dating someone?

88
00:07:32,041 --> 00:07:33,041
Huh?

89
00:07:34,257 --> 00:07:35,680
How can I be dating anyone?

90
00:07:37,924 --> 00:07:39,720
Forget it. I was just pulling your leg.

91
00:07:40,466 --> 00:07:42,003
- Good luck with your exam.
- Thank you.

92
00:07:49,965 --> 00:07:50,596
Here.

93
00:07:50,621 --> 00:07:51,621
Of course.

94
00:07:52,027 --> 00:07:55,480
Damn! The exam was so freaking difficult.

95
00:07:55,792 --> 00:07:57,543
Ms. Suda must still be mad at us?

96
00:07:57,696 --> 00:07:59,298
Please give her some credit.

97
00:07:59,588 --> 00:08:01,548
Ms. Suda only made the multiple-choice questions.

98
00:08:01,615 --> 00:08:03,456
Ms. Mai is responsible for the three
written-response questions.

99
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:04,608
GRADE 11, CLASS 7 Huh?

100
00:08:04,777 --> 00:08:05,777
Really?

101
00:08:05,822 --> 00:08:09,720
Oh, so she’s not as kind as I thought.

102
00:08:09,951 --> 00:08:11,204
Let’s go play football.

103
00:08:11,243 --> 00:08:12,760
- Come on. Let’s go.
- Damn it.

104
00:08:15,635 --> 00:08:17,360
Hey, you okay?

105
00:08:18,635 --> 00:08:19,635
I’m okay.

106
00:08:21,832 --> 00:08:22,960
Since we have time,

107
00:08:23,730 --> 00:08:25,360
wanna go get some egg yolk ice-cream?

108
00:08:26,245 --> 00:08:28,080
To celebrate you not moving abroad.

109
00:08:28,582 --> 00:08:29,326
Let’s go!

110
00:08:29,366 --> 00:08:30,629
- Come on, hurry.
- Go then.

111
00:08:33,547 --> 00:08:34,547
Hey, Kong.

112
00:08:34,683 --> 00:08:36,720
- Hey, what’s up?
- Wanna go get egg yolk ice-cream?

113
00:08:36,756 --> 00:08:37,640
Sure, why not?

114
00:08:37,707 --> 00:08:38,760
How are you doing?

115
00:08:38,997 --> 00:08:41,120
- Did you finish the exam?
- It finished me.

116
00:08:41,237 --> 00:08:42,560
Hey, where are you guys going?

117
00:08:42,810 --> 00:08:44,994
- To get egg yolk ice-cream.
- Hey, I’ll join you.

118
00:08:45,375 --> 00:08:46,680
Hey, Ked. Hey, Pim.

119
00:08:47,062 --> 00:08:48,360
Wanna go get egg yolk ice-cream?

120
00:08:48,524 --> 00:08:50,338
Yeah, sure. No basketball practice today.

121
00:08:50,369 --> 00:08:52,797
I’ll go, too. I don’t have extra classes today.

122
00:08:52,836 --> 00:08:55,400
Let’s go then. Are you waiting for your dads
to give permission?

123
00:08:55,572 --> 00:08:56,572
Kongpob!

124
00:08:58,337 --> 00:09:00,249
First one there eats for free. Last one pays!

125
00:09:00,308 --> 00:09:02,680
- Hey, wait!
- Go, go, go!

126
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:04,280
Come on. What are you waiting for?

127
00:09:04,758 --> 00:09:05,758
Let’s go.

128
00:09:15,538 --> 00:09:19,320
The students who just finished their exams
seem to be enjoying themselves.

129
00:09:19,928 --> 00:09:21,134
They’re laughing so loudly.

130
00:09:23,377 --> 00:09:26,520
Even now, after graduating, I still regret it.

131
00:09:27,210 --> 00:09:29,120
I should have had more fun back then.

132
00:09:40,504 --> 00:09:42,058
After presenting the flower garlands,

133
00:09:42,083 --> 00:09:46,323
MOTHER’S DAY CEREMONY, 2010
all mothers and student representatives from
each class, please take your seats.

134
00:09:49,955 --> 00:09:50,955
What did I draw, Ji?

135
00:09:51,414 --> 00:09:53,094
- A cat.
- Wrong, a bear.

136
00:09:54,365 --> 00:09:55,445
Enough with your old trick.

137
00:09:55,943 --> 00:09:57,160
And stop touching my back.

138
00:09:57,746 --> 00:09:59,953
Oh, you’re ticklish, aren’t you?

139
00:10:00,141 --> 00:10:01,592
- Take this!
- Hey.

140
00:10:02,679 --> 00:10:03,770
Hey, Tyler.

141
00:10:03,961 --> 00:10:06,040
Ty, knock it off.

142
00:10:06,277 --> 00:10:07,480
Stop acting like a child.

143
00:10:07,505 --> 00:10:10,200
Please, I saw you do the same thing on
Rose’s back.

144
00:10:10,909 --> 00:10:13,040
But did anyone make as much noise as you did?

145
00:10:14,573 --> 00:10:17,080
Don’t take it personally.
He’s said something worse to me.

146
00:10:20,042 --> 00:10:21,162
I’m bored, Ji.

147
00:10:21,542 --> 00:10:23,062
When can we get back to our classroom?

148
00:10:23,785 --> 00:10:26,800
Soon. They’re almost finished taking pictures.

149
00:10:26,862 --> 00:10:29,950
Next is the presentation of certificates to Outstanding Mothers

150
00:10:29,975 --> 00:10:32,720
of the 2010 academic year.

151
00:10:33,776 --> 00:10:37,200
Hey, look. That’s President Ruth’s mother, Ms. Orn.

152
00:10:37,763 --> 00:10:39,716
I knew it. Even from here you can tell
she’s beautiful.

153
00:10:39,740 --> 00:10:42,220
Ji, get down. I’ll take her picture for my dad.
He’s a big fan.

154
00:10:43,272 --> 00:10:44,578
Is she the president’s real mom?

155
00:10:44,962 --> 00:10:47,640
My grandma said she was abandoned
by her husband.

156
00:10:49,092 --> 00:10:51,732
But didn’t the president’s dad just come to school
to see Ms. Suda?

157
00:10:54,311 --> 00:10:56,760
That was a long time ago, even before we were born.

158
00:10:58,215 --> 00:11:00,680
The president’s mom was a famous actress.

159
00:11:01,039 --> 00:11:02,760
But she suddenly disappeared

160
00:11:03,067 --> 00:11:04,800
for over ten years.

161
00:11:05,648 --> 00:11:09,160
She said in an interview that she left to get
married and have three children.

162
00:11:09,904 --> 00:11:12,104
After that, the scandals surrounding her died down.

163
00:11:13,728 --> 00:11:16,920
I thought Ruth was an only child.

164
00:11:17,386 --> 00:11:21,240
Do you think his siblings’ names start
with an ‘R’ like his?

165
00:11:21,829 --> 00:11:26,880
If that’s the case, I’ll get tongue-tied trying
to say their names.

166
00:11:27,055 --> 00:11:29,538
No, his brother’s name is Khun and his sister’s name is Peach.

167
00:11:34,654 --> 00:11:37,365
Are you that close to him to know all that?

168
00:11:41,463 --> 00:11:42,595
I just saw it on the news.

169
00:12:01,785 --> 00:12:03,720
Ji, wait here. Don’t go have lunch without me.

170
00:12:03,794 --> 00:12:06,160
- I’ll be right back.
- Yeah, I know. Just hurry.

171
00:12:10,951 --> 00:12:11,951
Ji?

172
00:12:13,203 --> 00:12:14,680
Ji, is that you?

173
00:12:15,198 --> 00:12:18,240
Wow, you’re all grown up now.

174
00:12:19,196 --> 00:12:22,360
Ruth never told me you go to this school, too.

175
00:12:22,628 --> 00:12:25,920
How are Jira and Mon doing? I haven’t seen them for ages.

176
00:12:26,779 --> 00:12:27,779
Hmm?

177
00:12:29,189 --> 00:12:30,189
Uh...

178
00:12:30,214 --> 00:12:31,214
Ms. Orn.

179
00:12:31,532 --> 00:12:32,560
Your ride’s here.

180
00:12:33,102 --> 00:12:35,320
Come over to my house sometime.

181
00:12:35,539 --> 00:12:37,720
Your family has helped me so much.

182
00:12:37,880 --> 00:12:38,880
Okay?

183
00:12:39,843 --> 00:12:41,440
- Yes, ma’am.
- See you later.

184
00:12:43,090 --> 00:12:45,084
I’m off, Ruth. See you.

185
00:12:53,520 --> 00:12:56,560
- Why did your mom…
- Ji, let’s watch a movie today.

186
00:12:57,408 --> 00:12:58,440
Oh, hey, Ruth.

187
00:13:00,759 --> 00:13:01,680
What movie?

188
00:13:01,730 --> 00:13:03,057
Are we renting one from the video store?

189
00:13:03,081 --> 00:13:04,720
No, let’s go to the cinema.

190
00:13:05,094 --> 00:13:06,300
I was gonna go with my dad

191
00:13:06,325 --> 00:13:08,520
but he was busy so I asked you instead.

192
00:13:11,651 --> 00:13:12,580
What’s the movie?

193
00:13:12,624 --> 00:13:15,560
Umm, I don’t remember the title.

194
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:17,240
Oh, but I have the picture.

195
00:13:21,426 --> 00:13:22,480
A romantic movie?

196
00:13:23,783 --> 00:13:25,960
- Come on. Let’s go watch it.
- Can I come?

197
00:13:26,668 --> 00:13:27,760
You want to see it, too?

198
00:13:29,012 --> 00:13:30,012
I do.

199
00:13:31,146 --> 00:13:32,894
Don’t you have any student council work?

200
00:13:32,944 --> 00:13:34,363
I asked someone else to handle it,

201
00:13:34,721 --> 00:13:36,800
and there’s no meeting today either.

202
00:13:39,039 --> 00:13:40,039
Okay then.

203
00:13:40,077 --> 00:13:41,077
Yes!

204
00:13:41,124 --> 00:13:42,400
I’ll go invite the others.

205
00:13:42,860 --> 00:13:44,280
Ji, hold on to Ruth.

206
00:13:45,274 --> 00:13:47,040
In case he changes his mind. I’ll be back.

207
00:13:52,421 --> 00:13:53,421
Don’t let go.

208
00:13:53,859 --> 00:13:55,000
Or I’ll change my mind.

209
00:14:03,584 --> 00:14:06,176
Hey, Tawan. Hey, Lita, wanna go see a movie?

210
00:14:06,471 --> 00:14:08,760
Sorry, man. Well...

211
00:14:09,972 --> 00:14:11,520
We're going together.

212
00:14:13,824 --> 00:14:14,713
Hey, Pim. Hey, Ked.

213
00:14:14,763 --> 00:14:16,240
I've seen it with my family.

214
00:14:16,300 --> 00:14:17,300
Me, too.

215
00:14:17,748 --> 00:14:19,788
- Hey, Kong. Let’s go see...
- I hate romantic movies.

216
00:14:23,004 --> 00:14:24,760
At least there are three of us.

217
00:14:24,884 --> 00:14:26,947
- Are you sure you want to see it?
- Of course, Ji.

218
00:14:27,173 --> 00:14:28,762
Don't look down on romantic movies.

219
00:14:28,899 --> 00:14:30,920
No, that's not what I meant.

220
00:14:31,713 --> 00:14:33,160
Hey, the light’s green. Let’s go.

221
00:14:47,070 --> 00:14:48,670
Why don't we use the overbridge instead?

222
00:14:50,884 --> 00:14:52,240
But this is a crosswalk.

223
00:14:52,439 --> 00:14:54,344
There are traffic lights and an officer
directing traffic.

224
00:14:54,368 --> 00:14:55,568
It’s 100% safe.

225
00:14:56,337 --> 00:14:58,240
Umm, but...

226
00:14:59,358 --> 00:15:01,080
It'll be good exercise.

227
00:15:02,225 --> 00:15:03,522
Ruth is such a genius.

228
00:15:03,895 --> 00:15:04,895
Let's go.

229
00:15:16,626 --> 00:15:19,680
I'm excited. The last time I was at the cinema
was during summer break.

230
00:15:20,247 --> 00:15:22,520
Me, too. I usually watch movies on Netfli...

231
00:15:25,330 --> 00:15:26,092
Net?

232
00:15:26,149 --> 00:15:27,189
Net what, Ji?

233
00:15:28,944 --> 00:15:29,944
Net cafe.

234
00:15:30,284 --> 00:15:32,520
- At a Net cafe.
- Oh.

235
00:15:32,671 --> 00:15:33,791
At a Net cafe.

236
00:15:37,703 --> 00:15:38,604
It’s my dad, Ji.

237
00:15:38,676 --> 00:15:39,960
Hold on. Here, the tickets.

238
00:15:41,788 --> 00:15:42,788
Hello, Dad.

239
00:16:04,919 --> 00:16:06,240
Hello, test, test, Ji.

240
00:16:06,451 --> 00:16:08,880
My dad is free now, so he's coming after all.

241
00:16:09,027 --> 00:16:11,280
We're gonna have dinner and catch
the next showing.

242
00:16:11,502 --> 00:16:13,327
You and Ruth go ahead and watch the movie together.

243
00:16:13,351 --> 00:16:15,400
I’m so sorry.

244
00:16:15,466 --> 00:16:17,440
Take the popcorn money. It's my treat.

245
00:16:17,488 --> 00:16:19,080
- That’s it. Bye-bye.
- No, wait.

246
00:16:28,552 --> 00:16:30,000
- Uhh...
- It's time, right?

247
00:16:30,697 --> 00:16:31,760
You're not going in?

248
00:16:33,403 --> 00:16:34,483
You still want to?

249
00:16:34,766 --> 00:16:35,766
Eh?

250
00:16:36,739 --> 00:16:38,139
Don’t you want to watch it with me?

251
00:16:40,216 --> 00:16:41,840
Yes, but...

252
00:16:45,835 --> 00:16:47,355
But what? Let's go.

253
00:16:59,693 --> 00:17:00,693
Where’s the president?

254
00:17:00,733 --> 00:17:02,320
Watching a movie with Ji.

255
00:17:03,007 --> 00:17:06,200
Here. I ran into Mr. Tin and he gave me this.

256
00:17:06,725 --> 00:17:08,440
Can you pass it to Class 7?

257
00:17:23,930 --> 00:17:25,280
Oh, by the way,

258
00:17:25,688 --> 00:17:29,168
everyone in this picture has a nickname and
a real name that start with the same letter.

259
00:17:29,337 --> 00:17:31,349
Only Ruth is different.

260
00:17:31,746 --> 00:17:34,002
My name is Tawan Tontawan,

261
00:17:34,201 --> 00:17:36,134
and your name is Lita Lalita.

262
00:17:36,486 --> 00:17:38,078
The other five are the same, too.

263
00:17:38,644 --> 00:17:40,402
But Ruth Atiwitch...

264
00:17:43,516 --> 00:17:44,720
Oh, I just remembered.

265
00:17:44,817 --> 00:17:46,240
He used to go by another name.

266
00:17:50,791 --> 00:17:51,791
(Shone, )

267
00:17:52,992 --> 00:17:54,320
(I have something to tell you.)

268
00:17:56,413 --> 00:17:57,960
I really, really like you.

269
00:17:58,271 --> 00:17:59,600
It's been three years.

270
00:17:59,788 --> 00:18:02,360
I've tried everything.
I've improved myself just for you.

271
00:18:02,668 --> 00:18:03,668
(I…)

272
00:18:04,992 --> 00:18:08,589
(I can't imagine having someone like
that in my life.)

273
00:18:08,614 --> 00:18:10,174
(I’ve been studying hard just for you.)

274
00:18:10,302 --> 00:18:13,823
- (Someone who makes me want to be better.)
- (But now I know what I should do.)

275
00:18:13,848 --> 00:18:15,790
(What I should have done a long time ago.)

276
00:18:16,241 --> 00:18:18,194
(I want to tell you in person…)

277
00:18:19,490 --> 00:18:20,666
That I like you, Shone.

278
00:18:32,624 --> 00:18:33,624
(Oh.)

279
00:18:34,636 --> 00:18:35,685
(Maybe not.)

280
00:18:47,677 --> 00:18:49,120
(You and Pin are dating.)

281
00:18:51,656 --> 00:18:52,936
(You’re perfect for each other.)

282
00:18:53,814 --> 00:18:55,014
(How adorable.)

283
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:01,680
(I wish you both happiness.)

284
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:34,822
LUCKY DRAW

285
00:19:35,371 --> 00:19:36,680
Boy Come on, come on.

286
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:38,080
SCIENCE PROJECT

287
00:19:38,371 --> 00:19:40,838
Chrysanthemum tea! Chrysanthemum tea!

288
00:19:41,021 --> 00:19:43,200
Chrysanthemum tea! Chrysanthemum tea!

289
00:19:43,420 --> 00:19:46,080
Giving you refreshment and diabetes.

290
00:19:46,122 --> 00:19:47,840
Yay!

291
00:19:47,947 --> 00:19:49,122
Special price.

292
00:19:49,167 --> 00:19:51,831
First cup, five baht. The next one is 20 bath.

293
00:19:51,973 --> 00:19:53,440
Yay!

294
00:19:53,639 --> 00:19:54,639
Ugh.

295
00:19:54,931 --> 00:19:56,000
They’re driving me crazy.

296
00:19:56,380 --> 00:19:57,960
It’s okay. Let them be.

297
00:19:58,258 --> 00:20:01,720
I think since we’ve had them as promoters,

298
00:20:02,196 --> 00:20:03,440
our sales have gone up.

299
00:20:04,037 --> 00:20:05,120
- Really?
- Don’t you think?

300
00:20:06,491 --> 00:20:08,691
Hey, is Ty skipping school today?

301
00:20:08,946 --> 00:20:11,267
I thought he was only taking half a day off
to pick his dad up from the airport.

302
00:20:11,291 --> 00:20:13,171
I don't know. Maybe he just went straight home.

303
00:20:14,060 --> 00:20:16,860
Ji, why don't you take a break?
You've been working since this morning.

304
00:20:17,138 --> 00:20:18,880
Let the others take over in the afternoon.

305
00:20:19,049 --> 00:20:20,049
It's fine.

306
00:20:20,519 --> 00:20:22,200
No, it's not.

307
00:20:22,441 --> 00:20:24,040
You seem quiet without Tyler.

308
00:20:24,337 --> 00:20:25,977
Why don't you go take a walk by yourself?

309
00:20:26,514 --> 00:20:28,080
If you don't know where to go,

310
00:20:28,533 --> 00:20:30,481
go to the president's room to get a fake wound.

311
00:20:40,166 --> 00:20:42,560
See? Your hands are tired.

312
00:20:43,430 --> 00:20:44,470
Let me do it.

313
00:20:45,447 --> 00:20:46,447
Go take a break.

314
00:20:48,244 --> 00:20:50,560
- Say 'Chrysanthemum' first.
- Oh.

315
00:20:50,669 --> 00:20:52,582
- Let’s get more customers.
- Okay, okay.

316
00:20:52,621 --> 00:20:54,294
Chrysanthemum tea.

317
00:20:54,867 --> 00:20:55,804
(Come on and try.)

318
00:20:55,831 --> 00:20:56,920
(Hey, you want some?)

319
00:21:00,173 --> 00:21:01,173
Jiraphat.

320
00:21:01,624 --> 00:21:03,252
You're lonely without Tyler, huh?

321
00:21:03,572 --> 00:21:05,200
Wanna go get a fake wound in my class?

322
00:21:06,203 --> 00:21:07,400
We're almost out of supplies.

323
00:21:07,494 --> 00:21:10,040
Get it before it's too late.

324
00:21:15,149 --> 00:21:16,840
I don't see the Class 1 booth.

325
00:21:17,067 --> 00:21:20,280
Our booth is in the lab on the second floor
of the new building.

326
00:21:20,722 --> 00:21:21,760
Why is it there?

327
00:21:21,881 --> 00:21:24,200
What can I say? Our class is VIP.

328
00:21:25,241 --> 00:21:26,680
Just tell him the truth.

329
00:21:27,068 --> 00:21:28,535
Our materials stink like hell.

330
00:21:28,634 --> 00:21:30,720
So the teacher told us to move there.

331
00:21:30,873 --> 00:21:33,520
Don't tell him that. We'll lose a customer.

332
00:21:33,670 --> 00:21:36,500
It's not that bad, Ji.
The glue just smells a bit intense.

333
00:21:36,590 --> 00:21:38,660
But I've covered it up with some spray.

334
00:21:38,716 --> 00:21:40,877
Mr. Narong's ancient flower spray?

335
00:21:41,261 --> 00:21:42,480
Ugh, Tawan.

336
00:21:42,758 --> 00:21:44,240
Stop killing my vibe.

337
00:21:44,943 --> 00:21:48,000
Just go, Ji. Let the president make you
a fake wound.

338
00:21:48,218 --> 00:21:49,557
Tender hands. Excellent work.

339
00:21:49,637 --> 00:21:50,960
Guaranteed by Lita.

340
00:21:54,113 --> 00:21:55,880
Fine, I’ll go.

341
00:21:57,091 --> 00:21:58,600
Where's the lab again? Second floor?

342
00:22:02,071 --> 00:22:04,191
If you want to get a fake wound,
please come this way.

343
00:22:07,597 --> 00:22:09,110
This room might smell a bit strong.
FRIDAY, FEBRUARY 11

344
00:22:09,134 --> 00:22:10,320
Put the mask on.

345
00:22:24,019 --> 00:22:25,440
Hi, Ji, the good boy.

346
00:22:26,479 --> 00:22:27,480
Here to get a fake wound?

347
00:22:28,021 --> 00:22:29,021
Mmm.

348
00:22:29,722 --> 00:22:31,800
Oh, I forgot. I’m Ploy.

349
00:22:32,853 --> 00:22:33,853
Cinderella.

350
00:22:34,049 --> 00:22:35,049
Hey.

351
00:22:35,086 --> 00:22:36,098
You remember me?

352
00:22:36,188 --> 00:22:38,120
Of course. You were the star.

353
00:22:47,751 --> 00:22:49,200
Do you want to do Ji?

354
00:22:59,897 --> 00:23:01,320
The president is free now.

355
00:23:01,721 --> 00:23:04,480
You should have him do it.

356
00:23:05,889 --> 00:23:11,440
Having someone you’re close with do it
might be more… comfortable, right?

357
00:23:20,012 --> 00:23:21,080
I’ll finish this one.

358
00:23:22,601 --> 00:23:23,601
Hi.

359
00:23:24,420 --> 00:23:25,420
Hi.

360
00:23:27,883 --> 00:23:28,883
Give me your hand.

361
00:23:30,040 --> 00:23:31,040
Huh?

362
00:23:31,238 --> 00:23:33,118
It’s easiest to do it on the back of your hand.

363
00:23:34,713 --> 00:23:36,000
Oh, okay.

364
00:23:46,967 --> 00:23:48,560
It shouldn’t hurt at all.

365
00:23:49,656 --> 00:23:50,840
But if it does, tell me.

366
00:23:51,398 --> 00:23:52,480
I’ll be more gentle.

367
00:24:50,460 --> 00:24:51,460
It’s done.

368
00:24:53,514 --> 00:24:54,514
Wow.

369
00:24:54,958 --> 00:24:56,078
Looks so cool.

370
00:24:57,508 --> 00:24:58,508
You like it?

371
00:24:58,869 --> 00:24:59,869
Mmm.

372
00:25:00,124 --> 00:25:01,124
Yeah.

373
00:25:09,486 --> 00:25:10,520
Wanna take a walk?

374
00:25:11,360 --> 00:25:12,360
Huh?

375
00:25:12,603 --> 00:25:13,417
You have time?

376
00:25:13,442 --> 00:25:16,040
You can take a break.

377
00:25:16,380 --> 00:25:19,415
I’ll have someone clean that up.

378
00:25:25,840 --> 00:25:27,120
SCIENCE PROJECT

379
00:25:34,752 --> 00:25:35,752
Need a hand?

380
00:25:39,802 --> 00:25:41,383
Lucky draw?

381
00:25:42,280 --> 00:25:43,360
- Wow.
- Come on.

382
00:25:49,638 --> 00:25:52,000
- I give up. It’s too hard.
- That’s okay.

383
00:25:57,591 --> 00:25:58,671
Are you uncomfortable?

384
00:25:59,236 --> 00:26:01,236
No, I got all this free stuff.

385
00:26:24,310 --> 00:26:25,310
Eat more.

386
00:26:25,963 --> 00:26:27,040
So you’ll grow up fast.

387
00:26:27,687 --> 00:26:28,687
Huh?

388
00:26:30,340 --> 00:26:31,400
Wanna go to other booths?

389
00:26:35,071 --> 00:26:36,320
What’s going on with him?

390
00:26:36,706 --> 00:26:37,706
The president.

391
00:26:37,747 --> 00:26:39,880
President, wanna make a gel candle?

392
00:26:40,090 --> 00:26:42,160
We’re almost out. I won’t charge you.

393
00:26:43,567 --> 00:26:45,296
Oh, don’t worry.

394
00:26:45,690 --> 00:26:49,000
I won’t charge either of you. Come take a seat.

395
00:26:50,093 --> 00:26:52,520
Sorry, these are all the materials we have left.

396
00:26:52,711 --> 00:26:55,120
Use them all you want.
Come get me when you’re done.

397
00:26:55,556 --> 00:26:56,556
Thank you.

398
00:26:57,635 --> 00:26:58,635
Come on.

399
00:26:59,496 --> 00:27:00,616
Let’s do this.

400
00:27:03,822 --> 00:27:04,822
- You want more?
- I’m good.

401
00:27:13,975 --> 00:27:14,975
Hey!

402
00:27:49,766 --> 00:27:51,440
They’ll take about ten minutes to set.

403
00:27:52,151 --> 00:27:54,160
Should we eat while waiting?

404
00:27:54,581 --> 00:27:56,021
I’ll have a donut.

405
00:28:03,983 --> 00:28:04,983
Is it good?

406
00:28:05,712 --> 00:28:06,880
Look at my teeth.

407
00:28:33,134 --> 00:28:34,134
Thank you.

408
00:28:41,182 --> 00:28:42,555
Mine looks terrible.

409
00:28:46,561 --> 00:28:47,681
Take this one.

410
00:28:48,409 --> 00:28:49,484
And give me yours.

411
00:28:50,558 --> 00:28:51,558
Huh?

412
00:29:03,008 --> 00:29:04,880
President, we have a meeting.

413
00:29:27,749 --> 00:29:28,749
(Oh?)

414
00:29:30,084 --> 00:29:31,960
(Maybe I’m not that naive.)

415
00:29:32,538 --> 00:29:33,538
(Maybe...)

416
00:29:36,257 --> 00:29:38,400
(I’ve known how I felt all along.)

417
00:29:39,750 --> 00:29:41,230
(I was just in denial.)

418
00:29:41,274 --> 00:29:45,000
My heart keeps calling your name

419
00:29:45,293 --> 00:29:48,040
Just hear what it says

420
00:29:48,143 --> 00:29:50,240
(The more time we spend together, )

421
00:29:50,538 --> 00:29:52,600
(the clearer everything is.)

422
00:29:53,467 --> 00:29:55,000
Right now

423
00:29:55,240 --> 00:29:57,760
Just having you to love is all I need

424
00:29:58,070 --> 00:29:59,697
I won’t ask for more

425
00:29:59,722 --> 00:30:02,800
Your eyes on mine, your hand in mine

426
00:30:02,885 --> 00:30:07,800
Your face always there in my sight

427
00:30:09,632 --> 00:30:13,360
Grade 11, you have to attend
the sports day meeting. Don’t leave yet.

428
00:30:15,542 --> 00:30:16,840
Don’t go home yet.

429
00:30:17,788 --> 00:30:21,402
- When will this year end?
- Keep your thoughts to yourselves.

430
00:30:21,518 --> 00:30:28,040
AHHHHH!

431
00:30:31,862 --> 00:30:34,608
(Somebody, help Jiraphat!)

432
00:30:35,013 --> 00:30:37,240
(Tyler, help me!)

433
00:30:38,238 --> 00:30:39,238
- Ji!
- Jeez.

434
00:30:39,997 --> 00:30:41,320
You scared me.

435
00:30:42,385 --> 00:30:44,200
What were you dreaming about?

436
00:30:44,713 --> 00:30:45,746
Should we just go home?

437
00:30:45,775 --> 00:30:46,775
No, we can’t.

438
00:30:46,840 --> 00:30:48,680
I heard Ji calling out my name in my dream.

439
00:30:48,993 --> 00:30:51,293
Ji must be so lonely right now without me.

440
00:30:51,584 --> 00:30:53,160
Hurry up, dad. Take me to school now!

441
00:30:55,269 --> 00:30:56,269
Ji.

442
00:30:57,037 --> 00:30:59,640
Who dared hurt my Ji like this?

443
00:31:02,709 --> 00:31:03,920
It’s a fake wound.

444
00:31:04,213 --> 00:31:05,384
Stop being silly.

445
00:31:07,586 --> 00:31:08,800
It smells really bad, Ji.

446
00:31:09,527 --> 00:31:11,567
Are you sure it’s a fake wound and not
a rotten one?

447
00:31:11,769 --> 00:31:13,120
Ruth did this for me.

448
00:31:13,648 --> 00:31:15,320
It can’t be something dangerous.

449
00:31:15,566 --> 00:31:17,360
Ruth is the most dangerous one.

450
00:31:17,581 --> 00:31:18,760
- What’d you say?
- Nothing.

451
00:31:18,980 --> 00:31:20,440
Let’s clean up our booth, Ji.

452
00:31:20,465 --> 00:31:21,865
We’ll have to go to the sports day meeting next.

453
00:31:21,889 --> 00:31:22,889
Go, go, go.

454
00:31:22,984 --> 00:31:23,984
Let’s go.

455
00:31:24,040 --> 00:31:25,320
We’re here to help.

456
00:31:25,636 --> 00:31:27,400
Oh, how nice of you.

457
00:31:27,507 --> 00:31:29,446
If you’re gonna come this late,
why don’t you come tomorrow?

458
00:31:29,470 --> 00:31:31,537
Please, you’re making me blush.

459
00:31:31,823 --> 00:31:33,829
- Lift it up, 1…2…
- 1... 2...

460
00:31:34,786 --> 00:31:35,899
- It’s not moving, Gun.
- No, no.

461
00:31:35,923 --> 00:31:37,400
- Why are you pushing it down?
- Why are you doing that?

462
00:31:37,424 --> 00:31:38,424
Oh, I’m so, so sorry.

463
00:31:38,489 --> 00:31:39,827
- Again, 1... 2... 3.
- Go, 1... 2... 3.

464
00:31:42,746 --> 00:31:44,924
Why are you lifting it with one hand
but pushing it down with the other?

465
00:31:44,948 --> 00:31:45,670
- Yeah.
- Oh, right.

466
00:31:45,695 --> 00:31:46,880
1…2…3!

467
00:31:51,779 --> 00:31:54,086
Why do I feel like you two aren’t helping?

468
00:31:54,569 --> 00:31:56,686
- Are you messing with me?
- You’re just weak, Gun.

469
00:31:56,711 --> 00:31:57,442
Are you messing with me?

470
00:31:57,480 --> 00:31:58,920
Everyone, wake up.

471
00:31:59,078 --> 00:32:00,649
May I have your attention?

472
00:32:01,007 --> 00:32:02,920
Pinch your friends who are sleepy.

473
00:32:03,690 --> 00:32:06,720
For the sports day next semester,

474
00:32:07,282 --> 00:32:09,920
Grade 11 students…have to do everything.

475
00:32:14,712 --> 00:32:15,712
Quiet.

476
00:32:18,988 --> 00:32:21,880
Each class, send someone to draw a team color.

477
00:32:22,706 --> 00:32:23,706
Class 1.

478
00:32:27,697 --> 00:32:29,000
Class 1, blue.

479
00:32:30,167 --> 00:32:31,430
Ji, which team color do you want?

480
00:32:31,454 --> 00:32:32,968
I don’t think there’s a difference.

481
00:32:33,270 --> 00:32:35,400
Oh, that’s not fun. Pick one color.

482
00:32:35,913 --> 00:32:36,913
Just one.

483
00:32:37,634 --> 00:32:38,634
Then…

484
00:32:39,861 --> 00:32:41,750
I’ll choose the same color as Kongpob’s class.

485
00:32:42,066 --> 00:32:43,200
Kongpob’s class?

486
00:32:43,768 --> 00:32:44,640
Class 9?

487
00:32:44,783 --> 00:32:45,783
Mmm.

488
00:32:45,860 --> 00:32:47,820
Don’t you want to be in the same team as Class 1?

489
00:32:49,397 --> 00:32:51,160
- Gotcha!
- Gotcha!

490
00:32:51,387 --> 00:32:53,280
There’re only two classes with the same color.

491
00:32:53,399 --> 00:32:55,749
- It can’t be that much of a coincidence, can it?
- (Class 6, red.)

492
00:32:55,773 --> 00:32:56,773
Who knows?

493
00:33:00,190 --> 00:33:01,406
Class 7, blue.

494
00:33:01,431 --> 00:33:02,431
Hey, Ji.

495
00:33:02,970 --> 00:33:05,130
We got the same color as Ruth, Tawan,
and Lita’s class.

496
00:33:05,589 --> 00:33:07,400
Are you sad?

497
00:33:07,999 --> 00:33:11,280
- That you’re not on the same team as Kongpob.
- Yeah, right.

498
00:33:11,324 --> 00:33:13,960
But at least you have your best friend Ruth
on your team.

499
00:33:14,287 --> 00:33:15,287
That’s nice, huh?

500
00:33:15,314 --> 00:33:16,314
Right, Ji?

501
00:33:21,824 --> 00:33:22,840
What’s the matter?

502
00:33:23,372 --> 00:33:24,381
Aren’t you happy?

503
00:33:25,081 --> 00:33:26,081
Yeah.

504
00:33:29,847 --> 00:33:32,040
Too bad we’re not on the same team.

505
00:33:32,420 --> 00:33:33,940
I’m lucky I don’t have you on my team.

506
00:33:36,639 --> 00:33:37,639
That’s hurtful.

507
00:33:38,084 --> 00:33:39,960
Now you have to buy me egg yolk ice-cream.

508
00:33:40,173 --> 00:33:40,786
Why should I?

509
00:33:40,829 --> 00:33:43,294
- I think the shop has closed by now.
- No way.

510
00:33:43,319 --> 00:33:45,320
Let’s have shaved ice across the street then.

511
00:33:45,867 --> 00:33:46,867
Your treat.

512
00:33:47,358 --> 00:33:48,800
Tyler, Kongpob.

513
00:33:49,503 --> 00:33:50,503
Yes?

514
00:33:50,589 --> 00:33:51,589
What?

515
00:34:03,822 --> 00:34:04,822
What is it?

516
00:34:08,624 --> 00:34:11,040
- What if…
- That means it’s a real story.

517
00:34:11,272 --> 00:34:13,440
Hey, Kong. Don’t interrupt him.

518
00:34:13,510 --> 00:34:14,510
Let him finish.

519
00:34:18,301 --> 00:34:20,120
Fine. It’s a real story.

520
00:34:22,014 --> 00:34:24,322
What would you say if I told you I’m…

521
00:34:27,311 --> 00:34:29,280
not interested in the opposite sex?

522
00:34:31,714 --> 00:34:33,960
Are you saying you like boys?

523
00:34:35,776 --> 00:34:36,960
You can say that.

524
00:34:38,659 --> 00:34:40,179
So you just wanted to ask us directly?

525
00:34:40,353 --> 00:34:42,433
You learned how to be direct from Tyler, didn’t you?

526
00:34:42,728 --> 00:34:45,480
I only asked because it’s the two of you.

527
00:34:53,400 --> 00:34:55,480
Let’s go get shaved ice.

528
00:34:56,526 --> 00:34:57,526
Hold on.

529
00:34:57,706 --> 00:34:58,746
What now, Ji?

530
00:34:58,844 --> 00:35:00,560
Let’s go before the shop closes.

531
00:35:00,693 --> 00:35:01,960
You guys are okay with that?

532
00:35:03,774 --> 00:35:05,120
Okay with what?

533
00:35:05,342 --> 00:35:06,460
Why does it matter?

534
00:35:07,458 --> 00:35:08,800
I love my dad so much, Ji.

535
00:35:09,829 --> 00:35:11,880
What does your dad have to do with this?

536
00:35:12,730 --> 00:35:15,360
Well…I was raied by two dads.

537
00:35:16,980 --> 00:35:20,960
My mom and Dad Yai got divorced
when I was one year old.

538
00:35:21,710 --> 00:35:24,480
And a few years ago, before I moved to Thailand,

539
00:35:24,896 --> 00:35:26,960
Dad Yai had just legally married Dad Jiew.

540
00:35:32,633 --> 00:35:34,520
I’ve never told you that?

541
00:35:34,956 --> 00:35:36,240
No, you haven’t.

542
00:35:37,971 --> 00:35:39,320
That’s what you worry about?

543
00:35:40,858 --> 00:35:43,240
I don’t have a problem with that, personally.

544
00:35:43,663 --> 00:35:47,920
But you don’t need to tell everyone that.

545
00:35:48,549 --> 00:35:49,549
I know.

546
00:35:50,157 --> 00:35:52,680
Yay! Now that we got that out of the way,

547
00:35:52,839 --> 00:35:54,479
let’s go get some shaved ice, my friends.

548
00:35:54,685 --> 00:35:55,611
Let’s go!

549
00:35:55,700 --> 00:35:57,760
- Let’s go get shaved ice.
- Let’s go.

550
00:35:59,977 --> 00:36:02,160
Hey, I know, Ji.

551
00:36:03,990 --> 00:36:04,990
Know what?

552
00:36:05,379 --> 00:36:06,760
It’s Ruth, right?

553
00:36:08,971 --> 00:36:10,600
I’m not dumb, Ji.

554
00:36:11,417 --> 00:36:12,640
Ruth is nice.

555
00:36:13,237 --> 00:36:15,217
He’s smart. We can copy his homework.

556
00:36:15,776 --> 00:36:18,120
But today he hurt you while I was away.

557
00:36:18,570 --> 00:36:19,570
That’s not cool.

558
00:36:21,747 --> 00:36:22,880
Let’s go get shaved ice.

559
00:36:24,014 --> 00:36:25,374
Mali, be careful.

560
00:36:25,480 --> 00:36:27,920
Can you lift the left side up a little bit?

561
00:36:29,504 --> 00:36:30,760
Make sure it’s level.

562
00:36:34,483 --> 00:36:35,320
Good evening, Mom.

563
00:36:35,364 --> 00:36:36,520
Good evening.

564
00:36:37,385 --> 00:36:40,025
Why didn’t you sleep at school if you’re
gonna come home this late?

565
00:36:42,542 --> 00:36:43,542
What’s that?

566
00:36:43,653 --> 00:36:44,653
My gift?

567
00:36:48,626 --> 00:36:50,280
Eww, what’s this rubbish?

568
00:36:50,509 --> 00:36:51,760
Why is it so messed up?

569
00:36:54,294 --> 00:36:54,970
Oops.

570
00:36:55,062 --> 00:36:56,320
Ahem, mmm.

571
00:36:56,638 --> 00:36:59,722
So cute. It’s the cutest thing I’ve ever seen.

572
00:36:59,897 --> 00:37:01,840
Looks like it’s from the future.

573
00:37:03,153 --> 00:37:04,153
- Mom.
- Hmm?

574
00:37:04,361 --> 00:37:06,640
Tawan and Lita are having dinner here today.

575
00:37:06,932 --> 00:37:10,805
- We have a meeting about the sports day.
- Sure. I had the staff prepare lots of food.

576
00:37:14,499 --> 00:37:16,160
So, what do you think?

577
00:37:16,606 --> 00:37:18,320
Your dad won this painting at an auction.

578
00:37:18,636 --> 00:37:20,837
The artist who painted it has a son

579
00:37:20,862 --> 00:37:22,270
who goes to your school.

580
00:37:22,336 --> 00:37:24,680
His name is Tyler. Do you know him?

581
00:37:24,731 --> 00:37:26,440
Yes, he’s in the same class as Ji.

582
00:37:27,299 --> 00:37:28,299
Ji?

583
00:37:28,534 --> 00:37:30,200
Ji goes to your school, too?

584
00:37:30,633 --> 00:37:32,680
Why don’t you tell me? I’d love to see Jean again.

585
00:37:34,344 --> 00:37:35,880
Invite them for dinner sometime.

586
00:37:35,924 --> 00:37:37,040
Invite their whole family.

587
00:37:37,616 --> 00:37:40,840
- But what about dad?
- Mmm.

588
00:37:41,409 --> 00:37:43,440
Forget that crazy old man.

589
00:37:43,516 --> 00:37:45,158
I don’t know why he’s so arrogant.37.59

590
00:37:59,326 --> 00:38:01,680
Kong, will you help me with my report?

591
00:38:01,847 --> 00:38:04,280
What? I’ll go home right after I finish dinner here.

592
00:38:04,787 --> 00:38:06,400
What do you guys think this place is?

593
00:38:07,006 --> 00:38:08,046
A place to play with Mhee.

594
00:38:08,162 --> 00:38:09,962
A place to play video games and watch movies.

595
00:38:10,224 --> 00:38:11,800
That’s it. No movies today.

596
00:38:11,825 --> 00:38:13,320
Or I won’t finish my report.

597
00:38:14,844 --> 00:38:17,600
Let’s do something fun then.

598
00:38:19,299 --> 00:38:20,320
What’s wrong with you?

599
00:38:21,440 --> 00:38:24,120
I heard that the house next door is abandoned, right?

600
00:38:24,709 --> 00:38:25,840
How about a ghost hunt?

601
00:38:30,926 --> 00:38:32,680
That’s ridiculous.

602
00:38:33,334 --> 00:38:37,200
We’re gonna end up at the police station instead
for trespassing.

603
00:38:38,478 --> 00:38:40,158
You don’t have the guts.

604
00:38:40,203 --> 00:38:41,637
If you want to go on a ghost hunt,

605
00:38:41,798 --> 00:38:44,398
let’s check out the abandoned house
in the alley that burned down.

606
00:38:45,658 --> 00:38:47,456
Cool! Let’s go.

607
00:38:48,393 --> 00:38:51,560
If you’re not getting in, I’m gonna close the gate.

608
00:38:51,590 --> 00:38:54,520
- I’m gonna close the gate.
- Hey, hold on, hold on.

609
00:38:55,146 --> 00:38:55,892
Hey, hey, hey. Wait!

610
00:38:55,917 --> 00:38:57,557
- My shoes, my shoes.
- Take your shoes off.

611
00:38:58,559 --> 00:39:00,200
Hey, wait.

612
00:39:00,333 --> 00:39:01,600
Why are you here?

613
00:39:01,643 --> 00:39:04,440
Eh? It’s my house, too. Why can’t I be here?

614
00:39:04,562 --> 00:39:07,000
- Good evening.
- Good evening, beautiful Jean.

615
00:39:07,711 --> 00:39:08,751
Good evening.

616
00:39:08,824 --> 00:39:11,560
Ji, you should take him as an example.

617
00:39:11,790 --> 00:39:14,273
Stop being rude and be nicer to me.

618
00:39:14,296 --> 00:39:15,296
Here we go again.

619
00:39:15,713 --> 00:39:16,840
Hello, kids.

620
00:39:17,417 --> 00:39:18,823
- Hello, Mom.
- Good evening.

621
00:39:18,873 --> 00:39:20,360
Why are you back so early?

622
00:39:20,451 --> 00:39:22,640
- Dinner isn’t ready yet.
- It’s okay, ma’am.

623
00:39:22,752 --> 00:39:24,240
It’ll be worth the wait.

624
00:39:24,299 --> 00:39:26,560
That’s so nice of you, Ty.

625
00:39:26,669 --> 00:39:28,040
I’ll make you some cocoa.

626
00:39:28,104 --> 00:39:29,146
Can you make that two, please?

627
00:39:29,170 --> 00:39:30,664
I’ll make that three.

628
00:39:30,689 --> 00:39:32,080
Yes, three.

629
00:39:32,230 --> 00:39:35,360
Would you like your usual less-sweet cocoa, Kong?

630
00:39:35,483 --> 00:39:36,094
Yes, ma’am.

631
00:39:36,119 --> 00:39:37,960
- Take care of your friends.
- Okay, Mom.

632
00:39:39,512 --> 00:39:41,120
Will you drink all three cups?

633
00:39:41,201 --> 00:39:42,400
It’s just three cups, Ji.

634
00:39:48,768 --> 00:39:50,000
- Here.
- Thank you, ma’am.

635
00:39:50,122 --> 00:39:52,040
Your cocoa is the best in the world.

636
00:39:52,141 --> 00:39:53,640
Oh, you’re so nice.

637
00:39:53,822 --> 00:39:55,920
But I won’t make you another cup.

638
00:39:56,126 --> 00:39:59,280
You shouldn’t have too much sugar. Save some space for dinner.

639
00:40:00,184 --> 00:40:01,847
Jean, when we go to the mall tomorrow,

640
00:40:01,872 --> 00:40:04,533
remind me to buy more cocoa powder and coffee cups.

641
00:40:05,328 --> 00:40:07,728
- Okay.
- We’re running out of cocoa powder.

642
00:40:07,805 --> 00:40:11,280
- You remind me of young Ji.
- Jean, go help mom in the kitchen.

643
00:40:11,593 --> 00:40:13,440
No, I won’t. Why don’t you help her?

644
00:40:14,617 --> 00:40:15,657
If you won’t,

645
00:40:16,011 --> 00:40:17,880
I’ll tell mom about Dennis.

646
00:40:18,216 --> 00:40:19,216
Hey!

647
00:40:22,987 --> 00:40:25,000
- I hope Mhee bites you in the butt.
- Go on.

648
00:40:26,168 --> 00:40:27,960
Ty, excuse me.

649
00:40:28,381 --> 00:40:29,381
Please.

650
00:40:31,112 --> 00:40:32,112
Bye.

651
00:40:33,527 --> 00:40:35,480
Should we watch a movie while we wait?

652
00:40:35,983 --> 00:40:37,160
Hmm? What movie?

653
00:40:37,202 --> 00:40:38,560
We didn’t rent any.

654
00:40:38,758 --> 00:40:40,695
We can find one here.

655
00:40:41,596 --> 00:40:43,960
Those are my dad’s old movies.

656
00:40:44,137 --> 00:40:46,556
They’re so old you won’t find them entertaining.

657
00:40:46,586 --> 00:40:49,000
Yes, I will. They’re classic.

658
00:40:49,291 --> 00:40:50,198
Let me dig up one.

659
00:40:50,223 --> 00:40:51,223
Hey, wait.

660
00:40:51,957 --> 00:40:52,957
Oh, sh♪t!

661
00:41:00,123 --> 00:41:02,820
- I’m sorry.
- You sure are.

662
00:41:02,863 --> 00:41:04,080
Put them back now.

663
00:41:11,322 --> 00:41:12,480
What’s this, Ji?

664
00:41:14,451 --> 00:41:15,840
Looks like a photo album.

665
00:41:20,273 --> 00:41:21,273
Wow.

666
00:41:21,708 --> 00:41:22,800
If that’s Ji,

667
00:41:22,924 --> 00:41:25,640
this must be Jean, right?

668
00:41:25,967 --> 00:41:27,920
So beautiful. Ji looks cute, too.

669
00:41:27,993 --> 00:41:29,171
That’s enough, Tyler.

670
00:41:29,196 --> 00:41:30,080
Wait, Ji.

671
00:41:30,105 --> 00:41:32,320
- I don’t get to see this often.
- Hey, stop it.

672
00:41:32,403 --> 00:41:33,840
- Hey, Ji.
- Put it back.

673
00:41:34,197 --> 00:41:35,197
What’s that?

674
00:41:35,572 --> 00:41:36,572
What?

675
00:41:39,545 --> 00:41:40,600
Hey, let me see.

676
00:41:42,998 --> 00:41:43,998
Huh?

677
00:41:44,231 --> 00:41:47,000
Is this Ms. Ornrampha?

678
00:41:48,118 --> 00:41:49,560
How do you know her, Ji?

679
00:41:53,273 --> 00:41:55,960
How are we supposed to find anything in all these documents?

680
00:41:56,108 --> 00:41:57,040
Just keep looking.

681
00:41:57,116 --> 00:41:59,400
Last year’s records should be somewhere around here.

682
00:42:00,007 --> 00:42:00,760
Here.

683
00:42:00,818 --> 00:42:02,240
What? Did you find it?

684
00:42:03,072 --> 00:42:04,480
No, but I found this.

685
00:42:05,769 --> 00:42:06,800
What’s that?

686
00:42:06,904 --> 00:42:08,280
It’s not what we’re looking for.

687
00:42:08,633 --> 00:42:09,800
Look closely.

688
00:42:14,881 --> 00:42:16,840
Oh, this is…

689
00:42:17,844 --> 00:42:20,080
Wait, mom, come here.

690
00:42:21,924 --> 00:42:24,720
This is the photo I’ve been looking for.

691
00:42:25,278 --> 00:42:28,040
I told my friends I know Ms. Orn personally.

692
00:42:28,194 --> 00:42:29,720
But no one believed me.

693
00:42:29,899 --> 00:42:31,760
I’ll show them this picture.

694
00:42:31,917 --> 00:42:35,047
I was wondering where this photo album went.

695
00:42:35,513 --> 00:42:37,560
There’s something written in the back.

696
00:42:39,296 --> 00:42:40,600
Hey, Ji.

697
00:42:41,160 --> 00:42:44,520
MR. JIRA, MS. NARUMON, MS. ORNRAMPHA
JITRADA, JIRAPHAT, THEERARUTH, IRIN

698
00:42:44,544 --> 00:42:46,412
Dinner’s ready. Let’s eat first

699
00:42:46,437 --> 00:42:47,637
and then we’ll…

700
00:43:25,692 --> 00:43:28,400
(Hold my hand. Don’t let go.)

701
00:43:47,122 --> 00:43:48,643
(I don’t know what happened.)

702
00:43:49,376 --> 00:43:51,127
(I don’t know how I traveled back in time.)

703
00:43:54,440 --> 00:43:57,480
STUDENT COUNCIL, NAWINA SCHOOL
Class 7 won’t hand in their trays, right?

704
00:43:58,239 --> 00:44:01,120
(And it seems like Jiraphat)

705
00:44:01,799 --> 00:44:03,360
(has traveled back in time as well)

706
00:44:04,763 --> 00:44:06,640
You guys go ahead.

707
00:44:07,250 --> 00:44:08,400
I have to finish something.

708
00:44:09,210 --> 00:44:10,012
See you.

709
00:44:10,084 --> 00:44:11,520
(I’ll take this opportunity)

710
00:44:15,186 --> 00:44:17,880
(to do what my heart desires.)

711
00:44:32,892 --> 00:44:34,160
(And I won’t let Jiraphat)

712
00:44:35,747 --> 00:44:37,080
(end up the same way again.)

713
00:45:03,459 --> 00:45:04,819
I know the truth.

714
00:45:06,415 --> 00:45:07,415
The truth?

715
00:45:10,576 --> 00:45:13,560
(Maybe I didn't travel back in time to make new memories, )

716
00:45:13,656 --> 00:45:15,480
(or simply to remember things before I die, )

717
00:45:16,441 --> 00:45:19,951
(but to remember old memories I'd long forgotten.)
